From 59a3335a56879c8d1982c30f5e367062d4302330 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:40:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] PlaitOS: Settings icon styles and icons for the PlaitOS
 rows

- PlaitIconStyler (new code, inspired by crDroid's "Settings style"
  options): restyles row icons on every page and the home page tiles in one
  of seven styles (stock, colored or gradient background with a white
  symbol, accent or colored outline, colored or accent symbol), in a circle
  or rounded square, with stable per-row or random colors. Hooked where
  crDroid applies its own: SettingsPreferenceFragment.addPreferencesFromResource,
  the end of DashboardFragment's refresh and DashboardFeatureProviderImpl's
  tile icons. Style 0 (the default) leaves Settings exactly stock; app and
  account icons (bitmaps) are never restyled
- Options on the PlaitOS page, Misc tab > Settings style
  (plait_settings_icon_style, _corner_style, _random_colors; System);
  changing the style redraws the screen
- Every PlaitOS row gets an icon; the drawables come from crDroid's
  packages_apps_crDroidSettings (Apache-2.0), copied as ic_plait_*

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WNZzm3ssZ7eH5QDg4P9AiP
